            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "I reviewed all 22 manifest paths for security, data loss and unsafe input handling. I found no reachable, candidate-caused risk.",
              "Deletion in engine/skills/uninstall_plan.go is limited to the files an existing install record lists. PlanUninstall refuses an id with no install record or a procedural id before anything is planned. The id from the command line only selects a record. It is never used as a path.",
              "Data-loss guard: planSkill, install's planner, refuses the whole uninstall if any recorded file is edited, is not a regular file, or cannot be read. Tests in engine/skills/uninstall_plan_test.go and engine/cmd/skills_uninstall_cli_test.go pin that nothing is removed in those cases.",
              "RemoveEmptySkillDirs and removeEmptyTree in engine/skills/uninstall_plan.go call Remove only on directories that hold nothing but empty directories. A symlink is not a directory entry, so the code never follows it. It never deletes a file, so files the install record does not list are preserved, and the directory that holds them is reported as kept.",
              "engine/cmd/skills_install_cli.go takes the exclusive project lock before it reads or writes, as install does. The adapter refuses before locking when the working directory is not absolute.",
              "The recorded-path validation that applies to install records is in the base planner. It is not visible in this patch and not changed by it. I report nothing about it."
            ]
          }
        }
