            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "I found no candidate-caused reliability defect in the 22 changed paths.",
              "engine/skills/uninstall_plan.go reuses the install planner, so every refusal comes out before anything is removed. That covers an edited recorded file, a recorded path that is not a regular file, a file that cannot be read, an id with no install record, and a procedural id. engine/skills/uninstall_plan_test.go and engine/cmd/skills_uninstall_cli_test.go check that the tree is unchanged after each refusal.",
              "The dry run in engine/skills/app/uninstall.go writes nothing, and the CLI test compares the whole tree before and after.",
              "engine/skills/uninstall_plan.go leaves any file the install record does not list, and RemoveEmptySkillDirs reports the directory holding it as kept. A recorded file or runtime directory that is already gone is tolerated. Tests cover all three cases.",
              "engine/skills/lock.go makes the uninstall project lock exclusive. The CLI test checks that uninstall takes no overlay lock. A relative working directory is refused before any lock is taken, and the test checks that no lock file appears.",
              "The project-status change in engine/skills/app/project.go lists the install records and lets the id filter match a procedural skill or an installed one. The 'not in lock' error still fires only when neither matches, and a CLI test covers it.",
